# Yoruba (yo-NG) -- hunspell affix file
# Windows LCID 1130.
# Character inventory from An Crubadan project metadata (CC BY 4.0).
# 25-letter alphabet; no C Q V X Z.
# Mid tone is unmarked, so an unmarked word is not by itself an error.
LANG yo_NG
SET UTF-8
TRY aeiounbdgklmoprstwyhjfẹọṣáàéèíìóòúù́̀ńǹḿ

# Combining tone/dot marks must be word characters or hunspell
# splits words on them and never sees a whole token.
WORDCHARS ẹọṣẸỌṢáàéèíìóòúùÁÀÉÈÍÌÓÒÚÙ́̀'’-ńŃǹǸḿḾ

# MAP relates a plain letter to its marked forms. This is what makes
# an undiacriticised input get the correct suggestion while still
# being rejected as wrong.
MAP 12
MAP aáà
MAP eéè(ẹ)(ẹ́)(ẹ̀)
MAP iíì
MAP oóò(ọ)(ọ́)(ọ̀)
MAP uúù
MAP s(ṣ)
MAP AÁÀ
MAP EÉÈ(Ẹ)(Ẹ́)(Ẹ̀)
MAP IÍÌ
MAP OÓÒ(Ọ)(Ọ́)(Ọ̀)
MAP UÚÙ
MAP S(Ṣ)

# ICONV normalises legitimate non-NFC input onto the NFC forms held
# in the .dic: separately typed dot below, the vertical-line-below
# publishing convention, and tone typed before the dot.
ICONV 13
ICONV ẹ ẹ
ICONV ọ ọ
ICONV ṣ ṣ
ICONV Ẹ Ẹ
ICONV Ọ Ọ
ICONV Ṣ Ṣ
ICONV e̩ ẹ
ICONV o̩ ọ
ICONV s̩ ṣ
ICONV ẹ́ ẹ́
ICONV ẹ̀ ẹ̀
ICONV ọ́ ọ́
ICONV ọ̀ ọ̀

# Deliberately NO IGNORE directive: making tone and dot marks
# ignorable would accept undiacriticised text as correct, which is
# the exact failure this dictionary exists to prevent.

# No PFX/SFX yet -- add them with a morphologically analysed wordlist.
